  "body": "Part of #904. Notes from PR #911's high-tier review (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/911#pullrequestreview-5868416850) and #904's points 5 and 6 that #904's first slice did not take.\n\n1. **A stock copied from a coarse model loses its flag once that model is deleted.** `model_fidelity::coarse_source` finds the stock's excess by looking up its source model by name. With the source gone it reads 0, so the laws stop tightening for the same facets. The copy should carry the chord error itself.\n2. **A project saved before #911 with an over-budget mesh loads as full fidelity,** with no re-check. Decide: re-measure on load, flag \"fidelity unknown\", or leave it and say so.\n3. **Near the refusal edge the program sim can show a false gouge line instead of the named refusal.** Find the case and make the refusal win.\n4. **Display tolerances still read the plain 0.01 mm on a reduced-fidelity model:** the machined-surface classes (`machined_classes.rs`) and the viewport preview (`ui` `trace/eye.rs`, `cpu_eye.rs`). The binding verdict is tightened; the colours are not.\n\n**Done means:** 1 is fixed with a pin (delete the source, the stock's operations are still tightened or refused); 2 and 3 are each fixed with a pin or closed with the reason recorded; 4 is built or closed with the reason.\n",
